  "html": "<h2 id=\"multi-region\">1. Multi-Region Architecture</h2>\n  <figure class=\"dgfig awsfig\"><img class=\"aws-img\" src=\"/images/aws-sap/sap-s12-01-global-multi-region-application-architecture.svg\" alt=\"Global multi-region application architecture\" width=\"848\" height=\"624\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"min-width:640px;max-width:848px\"></figure>\n\n  <h3>Multi-Region Design Considerations</h3>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Data consistency:</strong> DynamoDB Global Tables = multi-active, eventually consistent. Aurora Global = active-passive, consistent.</li>\n    <li><strong>Session state:</strong> Use DynamoDB or ElastiCache for distributed session (not local memory)</li>\n    <li><strong>DNS TTL:</strong> Low TTL (30-60s) for faster failover. Higher TTL reduces DNS query load.</li>\n    <li><strong>Cost:</strong> Inter-region data transfer charges apply. Design to minimize cross-region data movement.</li>\n    <li><strong>Compliance:</strong> Data sovereignty laws may restrict where data can be stored. Use SCPs to prevent data leaving approved regions.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2 id=\"multi-account\">2. Enterprise Multi-Account Architecture</h2>\n  <figure class=\"dgfig awsfig\"><img class=\"aws-img\" src=\"/images/aws-sap/sap-s12-02-enterprise-multi-account-landing-zone.svg\" alt=\"Enterprise multi-account landing zone\" width=\"1022\" height=\"924\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"min-width:640px;max-width:1022px\"></figure>\n\n  <h2 id=\"saas\">3. SaaS Multi-Tenant Architecture</h2>\n  <figure class=\"dgfig awsfig\"><img class=\"aws-img\" src=\"/images/aws-sap/sap-s12-03-saas-multi-tenant-patterns.svg\" alt=\"SaaS multi-tenant patterns\" width=\"1398\" height=\"747\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"min-width:640px;max-width:1398px\"></figure>\n\n  <h2 id=\"serverless\">4. Serverless Architecture Pattern</h2>\n  <figure class=\"dgfig awsfig\"><img class=\"aws-img\" src=\"/images/aws-sap/sap-s12-04-enterprise-serverless-architecture.svg\" alt=\"Enterprise serverless architecture\" width=\"936\" height=\"832\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"min-width:640px;max-width:936px\"></figure>\n\n  <h2 id=\"containers\">5. Container Architecture Pattern</h2>\n  <figure class=\"dgfig awsfig\"><img class=\"aws-img\" src=\"/images/aws-sap/sap-s12-05-enterprise-container-platform-on-eks.svg\" alt=\"Enterprise container platform on EKS\" width=\"810\" height=\"656\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"min-width:640px;max-width:810px\"></figure>\n\n  <h2 id=\"datalake\">6. Data Lake Architecture</h2>\n  <figure class=\"dgfig awsfig\"><img class=\"aws-img\" src=\"/images/aws-sap/sap-s12-06-enterprise-data-lake-on-aws.svg\" alt=\"Enterprise data lake on AWS\" width=\"898\" height=\"776\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"min-width:640px;max-width:898px\"></figure>\n\n  <h2 id=\"global\">7. Global Application Architecture</h2>\n  <figure class=\"dgfig awsfig\"><img class=\"aws-img\" src=\"/images/aws-sap/sap-s12-07-global-application-with-low-latency.svg\" alt=\"Global application with low latency\" width=\"900\" height=\"831\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"min-width:640px;max-width:900px\"></figure>\n\n  <h2>8. Analytics Architecture</h2>\n  <figure class=\"dgfig awsfig\"><img class=\"aws-img\" src=\"/images/aws-sap/sap-s12-08-real-time-and-batch-analytics-architecture.svg\" alt=\"Real-time and batch analytics architecture\" width=\"1044\" height=\"763\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"min-width:640px;max-width:1044px\"></figure>\n\n  <h2 id=\"exam-tips\">9. Exam Tips</h2>\n  <div class=\"exam-box\">\n    <h4>SAP-C02 Advanced Architecture — Key Points</h4>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Multi-Region DB:</strong> Active/Active writes → DynamoDB Global Tables. Active/Passive → Aurora Global.</li>\n      <li><strong>SaaS isolation:</strong> Silo = separate stack (expensive but isolated). Pool = shared (cheaper, noisy neighbor). Bridge = hybrid.</li>\n      <li><strong>Serverless cost:</strong> Pay per request, zero when idle. Best for event-driven, variable traffic.</li>\n      <li><strong>IRSA (IAM Roles for Service Accounts):</strong> Pod-level AWS credentials in EKS — not instance profile.</li>\n      <li><strong>Lake Formation:</strong> Column/row level security on data lake. Controls Athena and Redshift Spectrum access.</li>\n      <li><strong>Kinesis vs SQS:</strong> Kinesis = ordered streaming, replay, multiple consumers. SQS = queue, one consumer per message.</li>\n      <li><strong>AppFlow:</strong> No-code integration for SaaS to S3/Redshift (Salesforce, ServiceNow, etc.).</li>\n      <li><strong>Global Accelerator vs CloudFront:</strong> GA = TCP/UDP, static IPs. CF = HTTP/HTTPS, caching.</li>\n      <li><strong>Glue vs EMR:</strong> Glue = serverless Spark ETL (simpler). EMR = managed Hadoop/Spark cluster (more control, larger workloads).</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"cheat-grid\">\n    <div class=\"cheat-card\">\n      <h5>Architecture Patterns</h5>\n      <ul>\n        <li>Event-driven: EventBridge + SQS + Lambda</li>\n        <li>CQRS: DynamoDB writes + ElastiCache reads</li>\n        <li>SAGA: Step Functions distributed txn</li>\n        <li>Strangler Fig: gradual monolith→micro</li>\n        <li>BFF: API Gateway per client type</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"cheat-card\">\n      <h5>Data Services Quick Ref</h5>\n      <ul>\n        <li>Streaming ingest: Kinesis</li>\n        <li>ETL: Glue</li>\n        <li>Ad-hoc SQL on S3: Athena</li>\n        <li>Data warehouse: Redshift</li>\n        <li>BI dashboards: QuickSight</li>\n        <li>ML: SageMaker</li>\n        <li>Search: OpenSearch</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"cheat-card\">\n      <h5>Container Platform</h5>\n      <ul>\n        <li>Simple containers: ECS + Fargate</li>\n        <li>Kubernetes: EKS</li>\n        <li>Pod IAM: IRSA</li>\n        <li>Image registry: ECR</li>\n        <li>Auto-scaling: Karpenter (EKS)</li>\n        <li>Service mesh: AWS App Mesh</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"cheat-card\">\n      <h5>Global Delivery</h5>\n      <ul>\n        <li>HTTP content: CloudFront</li>\n        <li>TCP/UDP perf: Global Accelerator</li>\n        <li>DNS failover: Route 53 Failover</li>\n        <li>Multi-region read: Aurora Global</li>\n        <li>Multi-active write: DynamoDB Global</li>\n        <li>Static assets: S3 + CloudFront</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </div>"
